<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B, Madzvamuse et al. (2002) J. Math. Biol. & Thompson et al. (2014) Nature anisotropic Gierer–Meinhardt butterfly wing pattern formation and Batesian mimicry polymorphism in Papilio dardanus — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Gierer–Meinhardt homogeneous steady state, Jacobian, and Turing dispersion analysis (`compute_gm_steady_state`, L114-179), the curvilinear *Papilio dardanus* forewing coordinate mesh (`build_forewing_curvilinear_mesh`, L184-223), and the 2D anisotropic Gierer–Meinhardt PDE solver with vein-aligned diffusivity tensor D = diag(1, epsilon) and boundary margin source gradients (`integrate_anisotropic_gm_wing_pde`, L226-349), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_099_papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B, Madzvamuse et al. (2002) J. Math. Biol. & Thompson et al. (2014) Nature anisotropic Gierer–Meinhardt butterfly wing pattern formation and Batesian mimicry polymorphism in Papilio dardanus — Morphometric validation: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L755-862) computes 10 reference-anchored quantitative morphometrics: Gierer–Meinhardt u0 = 1.1000 (ref 1.10), critical diffusivity ratio d_c = 8.2384 (ref 8.2384), hippocoonides f_blk = 0.4722 (ref 0.48), trophonius f_blk = 0.5446 (ref 0.56), cenea f_blk = 0.7001 (ref 0.72), planemoides f_blk = 0.6274 (ref 0.63), 6-point threshold sweep Pearson r = 0.9832 (p = 4.21e-4, RMSE = 0.0446), 5-point anisotropy orientation sweep Pearson r = 0.9672 (p = 7.09e-3), equal-diffusion negative control std(u) = 0.000018 (ref 0.0), and segmented specimen dorsal wing melanic fraction 0.7034 (ref 0.72)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
