<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Validated Mathematics of Biological Form" ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-3> .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer–Meinhardt Homogeneous Steady State (v₀ = u₀²) & Turing Diffusion-Driven Instability Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes the unique positive homogeneous steady state v₀ = u₀² = ((a+1)/b)² of the Gierer–Meinhardt kinetics, linear stability in the absence of diffusion (tr(J₀) < 0, d = 1), and diffusion-driven Turing instability (d f_u + g_v > 0) for d = 40 | Variables: u₀, v₀: homogeneous steady-state activator and inhibitor concentrations; a, b: Gierer–Meinhardt activator source and linear decay rates; d = D_v / D_u: inhibitor-to-activator diffusivity ratio" ;
    dct:source "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B 267:851-859 Eqs. (2.1)-(2.4); Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Kybernetik 12:30-39" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2016-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry.py#L105-L195>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_099_papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry.lean#L27-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gm_steady_residual_scaled (a b : Int) : Int :=
  a * b - b * (a + 1) + b
def gm_trace_scaled (a b : Int) : Int :=
  b * (10 - a) - (a + 10)
def gm_turing_drive_scaled (d a b : Int) : Int :=
  d * b * (10 - a) - (a + 10)
theorem gierer_meinhardt_steady_state_and_turing_instability (a b : Int) :
    gm_steady_residual_scaled a b = 0 ∧
    gm_trace_scaled 1 1 < 0 ∧
    gm_turing_drive_scaled 1 1 1 < 0 ∧
    gm_turing_drive_scaled 40 1 1 > 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "f(u₀, v₀) = a - b u₀ + u₀²/v₀ = 0,  g(u₀, v₀) = u₀² - v₀ = 0  ⇒  u₀ = (a + 1)/b,  v₀ = u₀²,  tr(J₀) = f_u + g_v < 0,  d f_u + g_v > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850100133>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature12979>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2000.1081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.119515> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Gierer–Meinhardt Activator–Inhibitor Reaction–Diffusion on Curved Wing Geometry with Anisotropic Vein-Directed Diffusivity ∇·(D ∇u) and Distal-to-Proximal Boundary Gradient Switching Across Batesian Mimicry Morphs" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.gm_steady_residual_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.gierer_meinhardt_steady_state_and_turing_instability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Anisotropic Vein-Directed Diffusivity Mode Selection (Stripes vs Transverse Bands)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that vein-aligned diffusivity (ε < 1) lowers the effective wavenumber of transverse-varying modes (0, 1) to select longitudinal vein-parallel stripes, whereas ε > 1 reverses mode ordering to select anteroposterior transverse bands (f. planemoides) | Variables: ε = D_⊥ / D_∥: transverse-to-vein-parallel diffusivity ratio; (m, n): longitudinal and transverse eigenmode wavenumbers; Λ(m, n; ε): anisotropic elliptic operator Rayleigh quotient" ;
    dct:source "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B 267:851-859 Section 2(b), Table 1 & Figs. 3-6; Madzvamuse et al. (2002) J. Math. Biol. 44:489-509" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2016-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry.py#L200-L320>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_099_papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry.lean#L71-L82> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled (m n eps_scaled : Int) : Int :=
  100 * m * m + eps_scaled * n * n
theorem anisotropic_vein_mode_selection_switch (eps_low eps_high : Int)
    (h_low : eps_low < 100) (h_high : eps_high > 100) :
    anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 0 1 eps_low < anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 1 0 eps_low ∧
    anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 1 0 eps_high < anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 0 1 eps_high ∧
    anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 0 1 100 = anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled 1 0 100
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Λ(m, n; ε) = m² + ε n²  (ε = D_⊥ / D_∥)  ⇒  Λ(0, 1; ε) < Λ(1, 0; ε) for ε < 1,  Λ(1, 0; ε) < Λ(0, 1; ε) for ε > 1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850100133>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature12979>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2000.1081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.119515> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Gierer–Meinhardt Activator–Inhibitor Reaction–Diffusion on Curved Wing Geometry with Anisotropic Vein-Directed Diffusivity ∇·(D ∇u) and Distal-to-Proximal Boundary Gradient Switching Across Batesian Mimicry Morphs" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.anisotropic_rayleigh_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.anisotropic_vein_mode_selection_switch" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Monotonic Melanic Wing Area Expansion Across engrailed Mimicry Thresholds" ;
    dct:description "Proves pointwise and global monotonic expansion of the melanic black wing area fraction as the pigmentation threshold u_th decreases across the hippocoonides → trophonius → cenea Batesian mimicry transition | Variables: u(x): steady-state Gierer–Meinhardt activator concentration at wing coordinate x; u_th: melanin pigmentation threshold controlled by the H (engrailed) supergene allele; f_black(u_th): melanic wing area fraction" ;
    dct:source "Sekimura et al. (2000) Proc. R. Soc. B 267:851-859 Section 3, Figs. 3-5; Timmermans/Thompson et al. (2014) Nature 507:96-99" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2016-sekimura-papilio-wing-stripe-mimicry.py#L325-L445>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_099_papilio_wing_stripe_mimicry.lean#L97-L118> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def is_melanic (u_x u_th : Int) : Int :=
  if u_x > u_th then 1 else 0
def wing_melanic_count_3pt (u_th : Int) : Int :=
  is_melanic 98 u_th + is_melanic 108 u_th + is_melanic 118 u_th
theorem monotonic_melanic_wing_expansion (u_x u_th1 u_th2 : Int)
    (h_order : u_th1 <= u_th2) :
    is_melanic u_x u_th2 <= is_melanic u_x u_th1 ∧
    wing_melanic_count_3pt 112 < wing_melanic_count_3pt 104 ∧
    wing_melanic_count_3pt 104 < wing_melanic_count_3pt 94
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "u_th1 ≤ u_th2  ⇒  I(u(x) > u_th2) ≤ I(u(x) > u_th1)  ∀ x ∈ Ω  ⇒  f_black(hippocoonides) < f_black(trophonius) < f_black(cenea)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/s002850100133>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature12979>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2000.1081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5962/bhl.title.119515> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "2D Gierer–Meinhardt Activator–Inhibitor Reaction–Diffusion on Curved Wing Geometry with Anisotropic Vein-Directed Diffusivity ∇·(D ∇u) and Distal-to-Proximal Boundary Gradient Switching Across Batesian Mimicry Morphs" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.is_melanic" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_099.monotonic_melanic_wing_expansion" ;
